    "note": "Version read: introduced bill (as filed), 2025-02-06. No votes recorded. The bill strikes the five-year expiry, the renewal process and the renewal fee ($75). Its Section 3 refers to cards issued 'after August 1, 2023', as printed; Section 5 uses August 1, 2025."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 3 (Minn. Stat. 624.714, subd. 7): A permit to carry a pistol issued under this section does not expire and permit cards issued after August 1, 2023, must prominently state that the permit does not expire.\nSection 2 (Minn. Stat. 624.714, subd. 3): The sheriff may charge an application processing fee in an amount not to exceed the actual and reasonable direct cost of processing the application or $100, whichever is less.\nSection 1 (Minn. Stat. 624.714, subd. 2a): An applicant must present evidence that the applicant received training in the safe use of a pistol within one year of the date of an application.\nSection 5: A person with a valid permit to carry a handgun issued under Minnesota Statutes, section 624.714, prior to August 1, 2025, shall request a replacement permit card that conforms with the requirements of Minnesota Statutes, section 624.714, subdivision 7, paragraph (c), prior to the expiration date listed on the permit holder's card.\nSection 5: The issuing sheriff may charge up to $10 to issue a replacement card under this section."
